        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Fourier transform - Wikipedia</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = {\n  tex: {\n    inlineMath: [['$', '$'], ['\\\\(', '\\\\)']],\n    displayMath: [['$$', '$$'], ['\\\\[', '\\\\]']]\n  },\n  svg: { fontCache: 'global' }\n};\n</script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-svg.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body {\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    background: #fff;\n    color: #111;\n  }\n  body {\n    width: 768px;\n    min-height: 994px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 12px;\n  }\n  .page {\n    position: relative;\n    width: 768px;\n    min-height: 994px;\n    padding-top: 19px;\n  }\n  .page-header {\n    position: relative;\n    height: 18px;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    line-height: 11px;\n  }\n  .timestamp {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 29px;\n    top: 0;\n  }\n  .source-title {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    right: 0;\n    top: 0;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n  h1 {\n    width: 684px;\n    margin: 0 0 10px 42px;\n    font-size: 15.5px;\n    line-height: 18px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .math-italic {\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n  table.formulas {\n    width: 684px;\n    height: 743px;\n    margin-left: 42px;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    table-layout: fixed;\n    font-size: 11px;\n  }\n  table.formulas col.num { width: 30px; }\n  table.formulas col.fn { width: 127px; }\n  table.formulas col.ft1 { width: 109px; }\n  table.formulas col.ft2 { width: 136px; }\n  table.formulas col.ft3 { width: 123px; }\n  table.formulas col.remarks { width: 159px; }\n\n  table.formulas th,\n  table.formulas td {\n    border: 1px solid #b7b7b7;\n    padding: 5px 6px;\n    overflow: hidden;\n  }\n  table.formulas th {\n    height: 53px;\n    text-align: center;\n    vertical-align: middle;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    line-height: 14px;\n  }\n  table.formulas td {\n    vertical-align: middle;\n  }\n  table.formulas td.num {\n    padding: 0;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 10px;\n  }\n  table.formulas td.function {\n    text-align: left;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n  }\n  table.formulas td.transform {\n    padding: 4px 3px;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n  }\n  table.formulas td.remarks {\n    padding: 5px 6px;\n    vertical-align: top;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    line-height: 15px;\n    text-align: left;\n  }\n  tr.r500 { height: 59px; }\n  tr.r501 { height: 230px; }\n  tr.r502 { height: 199px; }\n  tr.r503 { height: 139px; }\n  tr.r504 { height: 63px; }\n\n  .definition {\n    display: block;\n    text-align: left;\n    margin: 0 0 2px 2px;\n  }\n  .formula-line {\n    display: block;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .note-link {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 8px;\n    vertical-align: super;\n    text-decoration: underline;\n  }\n  .remarks em {\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n  }\n  .see-also {\n    width: 684px;\n    margin: 25px 0 0 42px;\n  }\n  .see-also h2 {\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0 0 1px 0;\n    border-bottom: 7px double #111;\n    font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n    font-size: 20px;\n    line-height: 22px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .see-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n    column-gap: 31px;\n    padding-top: 7px;\n  }\n  .see-grid ul {\n    list-style: none;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0 0 0 19px;\n  }\n  .see-grid li {\n    position: relative;\n    margin: 0 0 5px 0;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 18px;\n  }\n  .see-grid li::before {\n    content: \"▪\";\n    position: absolute;\n    left: -14px;\n    top: 0;\n    font-size: 11px;\n  }\n  .footer {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 29px;\n    right: 29px;\n    bottom: 18px;\n    height: 12px;\n    font-size: 9px;\n    line-height: 12px;\n  }\n  .footer .url { float: left; }\n  .footer .page-number { float: right; }\n\n  mjx-container {\n    margin: 0 !important;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n  <header class=\"page-header\">\n    <div class=\"timestamp\">2026/6/29 02:59</div>\n    <div class=\"source-title\">Fourier transform - Wikipedia</div>\n  </header>\n\n  <h1>Formulas for general <span class=\"math-italic\">n</span>-dimensional functions</h1>\n\n  <table class=\"formulas\">\n    <colgroup>\n      <col class=\"num\">\n      <col class=\"fn\">\n      <col class=\"ft1\">\n      <col class=\"ft2\">\n      <col class=\"ft3\">\n      <col class=\"remarks\">\n    </colgroup>\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th></th>\n        <th>Function</th>\n        <th>Fourier transform<br>unitary, ordinary<br>frequency</th>\n        <th>Fourier transform<br>unitary, angular<br>frequency</th>\n        <th>Fourier transform<br>non-unitary, angular<br>frequency</th>\n        <th>Remarks</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr class=\"r500\">\n        <td class=\"num\">500</td>\n        <td class=\"function\">$f(x)$</td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"definition\">$\\widehat f_1(\\xi)\\triangleq$</span>\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\int_{\\mathbb R^n}f(x)e^{-i2\\pi\\xi\\cdot x}\\,dx$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"definition\">$\\widehat f_2(\\omega)\\triangleq$</span>\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{(2\\pi)^{n/2}}\\int_{\\mathbb R^n}f(x)e^{-i\\omega\\cdot x}\\,dx$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"definition\">$\\widehat f_3(\\omega)\\triangleq$</span>\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\int_{\\mathbb R^n}f(x)e^{-i\\omega\\cdot x}\\,dx$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"remarks\"></td>\n      </tr>\n\n      <tr class=\"r501\">\n        <td class=\"num\">501</td>\n        <td class=\"function\">$\\chi_{[0,1]}(|x|)(1-|x|^2)^\\delta$</td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{\\Gamma(\\delta+1)}{\\pi^\\delta|\\xi|^\\gamma}\\,J_\\gamma(2\\pi|\\xi|)$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle 2^\\delta\\frac{\\Gamma(\\delta+1)}{|\\omega|^\\gamma}\\,J_\\gamma(|\\omega|)$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{\\Gamma(\\delta+1)}{\\pi^\\delta}\\left|\\frac{\\omega}{2\\pi}\\right|^{-\\gamma}J_\\gamma(\\omega)$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"remarks\">\n          Here, $\\gamma=\\frac n2+\\delta$.<br>\n          The function $\\chi_{[0,\\,1]}$ is the indicator function of the interval $[0,\\,1]$.\n          The function $\\Gamma(x)$ is the gamma function.\n          The function $J_{\\frac n2+\\delta}$ is a Bessel function of the first kind, with order\n          $\\frac n2+\\delta$. Taking $n=2$ and $\\delta=0$ produces 402.<span class=\"note-link\">[82]</span>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n\n      <tr class=\"r502\">\n        <td class=\"num\">502</td>\n        <td class=\"function\">$|x|^{-\\alpha},\\quad 0&lt;\\operatorname{Re}\\alpha&lt;n$</td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{(2\\pi)^\\alpha}{c_{n,\\alpha}}|\\xi|^{-(n-\\alpha)}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{(2\\pi)^{n/2}}{c_{n,\\alpha}}|\\omega|^{-(n-\\alpha)}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{(2\\pi)^n}{c_{n,\\alpha}}|\\omega|^{-(n-\\alpha)}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"remarks\">\n          See <em><u>Riesz potential</u></em>, where the constant is given by<br>\n          $\\displaystyle c_{n,\\alpha}=\\frac{\\pi^{n/2}2^\\alpha\\Gamma\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)}\n          {\\Gamma\\left(\\frac{n-\\alpha}{2}\\right)}$.<br>\n          The formula also holds for all $\\alpha\\ne n,n+2,\\ldots$ by analytic continuation,\n          but then the function and its Fourier transforms need to be understood as suitably\n          regularized tempered distributions (see <em><u>Homogeneous distribution</u></em>).<span class=\"note-link\">[note 10]</span>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n\n      <tr class=\"r503\">\n        <td class=\"num\">503</td>\n        <td class=\"function\">\n          $\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{|\\sigma|(2\\pi)^{n/2}}\n          e^{-\\frac12x^{\\mathsf T}\\sigma^{-\\mathsf T}\\sigma^{-1}x}$\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle e^{-2\\pi^2\\xi^{\\mathsf T}\\sigma\\sigma^{\\mathsf T}\\xi}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle(2\\pi)^{-n/2}e^{-\\frac12\\omega^{\\mathsf T}\\sigma\\sigma^{\\mathsf T}\\omega}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle e^{-\\frac12\\omega^{\\mathsf T}\\sigma\\sigma^{\\mathsf T}\\omega}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"remarks\">\n          This is the formula for a multivariate normal distribution normalized to 1 with a mean of 0.\n          Bold variables are vectors or matrices. Following the notation of the aforementioned page,\n          $\\boldsymbol{\\Sigma}=\\boldsymbol{\\sigma}\\boldsymbol{\\sigma}^{\\mathsf T}$ and\n          $\\boldsymbol{\\Sigma}^{-1}=\\boldsymbol{\\sigma}^{-\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol{\\sigma}^{-1}$\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n\n      <tr class=\"r504\">\n        <td class=\"num\">504</td>\n        <td class=\"function\">$e^{-2\\pi\\alpha|x|}$</td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{c_n\\alpha}\n          {\\left(\\alpha^2+|\\xi|^2\\right)^{\\frac{n+1}{2}}}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{c_n(2\\pi)^{\\frac{n+2}{2}}\\alpha}\n          {\\left(4\\pi^2\\alpha^2+|\\omega|^2\\right)^{\\frac{n+1}{2}}}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"transform\">\n          <span class=\"formula-line\">$\\displaystyle\\frac{c_n(2\\pi)^{n+1}\\alpha}\n          {\\left(4\\pi^2\\alpha^2+|\\omega|^2\\right)^{\\frac{n+1}{2}}}$</span>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"remarks\">\n          Here<span class=\"note-link\">[83]</span> $c_n=\\Gamma\\left(\\frac{n+1}{2}\\right)/\\pi^{\\frac{n+1}{2}}$,<br>\n          $\\operatorname{Re}(\\alpha)&gt;0$\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n\n  <section class=\"see-also\">\n    <h2>See also</h2>\n    <div class=\"see-grid\">\n      <ul>\n        <li>Analog signal processing – Signal processing conducted<br>on analog signals</li>\n        <li>Beavers–Lipson strip – Mathematical tool in<br>crystallography</li>\n      </ul>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Constant-Q transform – Short-time Fourier transform<br>with variable resolution</li>\n        <li>DFT matrix – Discrete fourier transform expressed as a<br>matrix</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <footer class=\"footer\">\n    <span class=\"url\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_transform</span>\n    <span class=\"page-number\">38/45</span>\n  </footer>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
